on.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"papers/19f39182ec849fb6d78c3399.json","pointer":"/manuscript"},"id":"p:A-counterexample-to-the-Monge-ansatz-for-the-three-marginal-Coulomb-cost-September-25-2026","name":"A counterexample to the Monge ansatz for the three-marginal Coulomb cost","status":"current"}],"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","producer_scope":{"credit":{"kind":"attributed-catalogue-extraction","license":"Apache-2.0","name":"Will Cook, OpenAI Math Atlas; source manuscripts and Lean quotations credited to OpenAI.","pin":"8056826bbd00caea871ad036bd295182e2bef3e2","producer_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","producer_repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","sha256":"sha256:2c90a33675d6e8a37b8ab7c2e2107f358dd73fbc4c74dc1e183c17efa0e16267","source":"data/families.json"},"state":"producer-declared","value":{"rows":[{"label":"Coulomb Monge nonattainment with equality of infima","statements":["CoulombCounterexample"]}],"scope":"The Monge ansatz asks whether an optimal multi-marginal transport plan can be induced by maps from one marginal. For the three-marginal Coulomb cost in $\\mathbb R^3$, the formalization constructs a smooth compactly supported probability density, with smooth compactly supported square root, for which no pair of measure-preserving Borel maps attains the Kantorovich minimum.\n\nNevertheless, the Monge and Kantorovich infima are equal: preserving maps with finite costs approach the minimum. This is the three-dimensional Coulomb result; the paper's inverse-power extensions in every dimension are outside this statement.","title":"Nonattainment of the three-marginal Coulomb Monge problem","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/373.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":"The inverse-power (Riesz s > 0) extensions in every dimension d ≥ 2.","note":null,"reading":"reading:d3dd00fd9bb40203b45a98bc","source_term":"NARROWER — DECLARED","state":"narrower"},{"definitions_to_check":"`invDistance x y := (ofReal ‖x - y‖)⁻¹` in ℝ≥0∞ (value ⊤ on the diagonal), `kantorovichValue`/`mongeValue` as ⨅ over couplings / measure-preserving map pairs; all standard","gap":null,"note":"`coulomb_counterexample_and_equal_infima`: there is a smooth compactly supported probability density ρ on ℝ³ (with smooth compactly supported √ρ) whose three-marginal Kantorovich problem for the cost Σ 1/|x_i-x_j| with identical marginals has finite value attained by some coupling, no pair of measurable measure-preserving maps (T₂,T₃) attains it, yet the Monge infimum equals the Kantorovich value and finite-cost Monge maps approach it. The summary's extension to every inverse-power Riesz exponent in each dimension ≥ 2 is not stated (docs: 'outside this statement').","reading":"reading:860c8b22710064fb283d9c06","source_term":"partial","state":"part"}],"readings":["reading:d3dd00fd9bb40203b45a98bc","reading:860c8b22710064fb283d9c06"],"state":"different-scope-descriptions"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"8056826bbd00caea871ad036bd295182e2bef3e2","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's headline, clause by clause. Decider: Comparator (leanprover/comparator d03acab1 = tag v4.34.0, built with the release's toolchain v4.34.1), lean4export 076e8e57, landrun 811cfff5, nanoda_lib 3a240721 — on GitHub's Linux runners 