eptember-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":29,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1d9454a4ed095ef8f0c760b24c456de7c09f50f5129594a026b2c960f63ba021","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-the-Monge-ansatz-for-the-three-marginal-Coulomb-cost-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:ee89a6c466e41f695f50012c1395fe0ca1f5052a18b05b7faa9f4d3ea44e4f7a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-counterexample-to-the-Monge-ansatz-for-the-three-marginal-Coulomb-cost-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L29"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is a nonnegative density \\(\\rho\\) on \\(\\R^3\\) such that\n\\[\n \\int_{\\R^3}\\rho(x)\\dd x=1,\\qquad\n \\rho\\in C_c^\\infty(\\R^3),\\qquad\n \\sqrt{\\rho}\\in C_c^\\infty(\\R^3),\n\\]\nwith the following properties. For \\(\\mu=\\rho\\dd x\\), the value\n\\(\\E(\\mu)\\) is finite and is attained by a coupling in\n\\(\\Pi(\\mu,\\mu,\\mu)\\), but every pair of Borel maps\n\\(T_2,T_3:\\R^3\\to\\R^3\\) satisfying\n\\((T_2)_\\#\\mu=(T_3)_\\#\\mu=\\mu\\) obeys\n\\[\n \\int_{\\R^3}c\\bigl(x,T_2(x),T_3(x)\\bigr)\\dd\\mu(x)>\\E(\\mu).\n\\]\nThe inequality permits the left-hand side to be infinite."},{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:0dde76f3c08490254072e5704e3b1eaa988f82843adfb6b36d05fa5b5b810f3f","grain":"paper-statement","id":"A-counterexample-to-the-Monge-ansatz-for-the-three-marginal-Coulomb-cost-September-25-2026#prop:certificate","title":"prop:certificate"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/d4